2
-- JOIN: both sides keep their own index stats (no flat aggregation under the join header).
-- { echo }
explain indexes=1, compact=1 select * from test_compact_a a inner join test_compact_b b on a.key = b.key where a.key > 15000 and b.key > 5000;
Output: key, value, key, value

Join (JOIN FillRightFirst)
│  a ⋈ b
│  Type: inner | Strictness: all | Algorithm: SpillingHashJoin(HashJoin)
│  Join conditions: key = key
│  Output:
│    Left:  key, value
│    Right: key, value
├──ReadFromMergeTree (default.test_compact_a)
│     Read type: Default
│     Parts: 1 | Granules: 5
│     Output: key, value
│     Prewhere filter
│     Prewhere filter column:  key > 5000 AND key > 15000
│     Indexes:
│       PrimaryKey
│         Keys:
│           key
│         Condition: and((key in [5001, +Inf)), (key in [15001, +Inf)))
│         Parts: 1/2
│         Granules: 5/20
│         Search Algorithm: binary search
│       Ranges: 1
└──ReadFromMergeTree (default.test_compact_b)
      Read type: Default
      Parts: 0 | Granules: 0
      Output: key, value
      Prewhere filter
      Prewhere filter column:  key > 15000 AND key > 5000
      Indexes:
        PrimaryKey
          Keys:
            key
          Condition: and((key in [15001, +Inf)), (key in [5001, +Inf)))
          Parts: 0/1
          Granules: 0/10
          Search Algorithm: binary search
        Ranges: 0
